sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / Data Scientist
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Webhook as Kueue Webhook Server<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS TLS
    participant Controller as Kueue Controller<br/>(watch via 443/TCP)
    participant Scheduler as Kueue Scheduler<br/>(in-process)
    participant Cache as In-Memory Cache
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS

    Note over User,Prometheus: Flow 1: Job Admission

    User->>K8sAPI: 1. Create Job with queue-name label<br/>Auth: User credentials (OIDC/cert)

    K8sAPI->>Webhook: 2. Admission Review (mutating)<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS, API server client cert
    Webhook->>Webhook: Default queue label, suspend job,<br/>set managedBy field
    Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admit (mutated)

    K8sAPI->>Webhook: 3. Admission Review (validating)<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS, API server client cert
    Webhook->>K8sAPI: Validate constraints<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, SA Token
    Webhook-->>K8sAPI: Admit (validated)

    K8sAPI-->>User: Job created (suspended)

    Note over Controller,Cache: Controller detects new Job via watch

    K8sAPI->>Controller: 4. Watch event: new Job<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, SA Token
    Controller->>K8sAPI: Create Workload CR<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, SA Token

    Controller->>Cache: Update cache with new Workload
    Controller->>Scheduler: Notify: new pending Workload

    Scheduler->>Cache: 5. Evaluate Workload against<br/>ClusterQueue quotas
    Note over Scheduler,Cache: Check: quota available?<br/>Check: priority & fair sharing<br/>Check: admission checks passed?

    alt Quota Available
        Scheduler->>Cache: Reserve quota, mark admitted
        Scheduler->>Controller: Admission decision: ADMIT
        Controller->>K8sAPI: 6. Patch Job: set suspend=false<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, SA Token
        K8sAPI-->>Controller: Job unsuspended, pods created
    else Quota Exhausted
        Scheduler->>Scheduler: Evaluate preemption candidates
        alt Preemption Possible
            Scheduler->>Controller: Preempt lower-priority Workload
            Controller->>K8sAPI: Evict preempted Workload
            Controller->>K8sAPI: Patch preempted Job: suspend=true
            Scheduler->>Controller: Admit new Workload
            Controller->>K8sAPI: Patch Job: suspend=false
        else No Preemption
            Note over Scheduler: Workload stays pending<br/>Requeued with backoff
        end
    end

    Note over Prometheus,Controller: Flow 2: Metrics Scraping

    Prometheus->>Controller: 1. GET /metrics<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS TLS, Bearer Token
    Controller->>K8sAPI: 2. SubjectAccessReview<br/>443/TCP HTTPS, SA Token
    K8sAPI-->>Controller: Authorized
    Controller-->>Prometheus: Metrics response<br/>(queue depths, admission latency, etc.)
